      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Missing `libusb_init` Error Handling:** In the `iapcontrol` constructor, `libusb_init(nullptr)` is called without checking its return value. If USB initialization fails (e.g., due to system resource exhaustion or permissions), the constructor silently continues, leading to an inevitable crash or undefined behavior down the line.\n\n**Remediation:** Check if `libusb_init` returns a non-zero error code. If it does, safely transition the class state to prevent `connectDevice` from running.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 68,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 68,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "eee15e6508ade570d3670bc2f00d613d0a77d9c7",
