      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Out-of-Bounds Crash in `readRomData`:** In `util/elan/iapcontrol.cc`, `writeRomData` correctly calculates the remaining chunk size using `std::min(pageSize, buff.size() - offset)`. However, `readRomData` fails to do this:\n\n```c\n// Current implementation\nauto chunk \u003d std::span(buff).subspan(offset, pageSize);\n```\n\n  If the firmware size is not perfectly aligned to `BOOT_PAGE_SIZE` (64 bytes), `subspan` will throw a `std::out_of_range` exception on the final loop iteration. **Remediation:** Apply the same boundary calculation used in `writeRomData`:\n\n```c\nauto chunk \u003d std::span(buff).subspan(offset, std::min(pageSize, buff.size() - offset));\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 537,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 537,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "eee15e6508ade570d3670bc2f00d613d0a77d9c7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
