      "writtenOn": "2026-04-23T00:21:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here\u0027s another way to solve this, which is a little cleaner. The code was generated by Gemini, so please review and test:\n\n```\n#include \u003cranges\u003e\n\nint iapcontrol::readRomData(std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e buff)\n{\n    const char funcName[] \u003d \"read data\";\n    size_t offset \u003d 0;\n    const size_t pageSize \u003d BOOT_PAGE_SIZE;\n\n    if (buff.empty()) return -1;\n\n    for (auto chunk : buff | std::views::chunk(pageSize)) {\n        if (iapRecvData(chunk)) {\n            logInfo(\"[IAP] {} - fail, count: {}\\n\", funcName, offset);\n            return -1;\n        }\n\n        offset +\u003d chunk.size();\n\n        if (m_progressCallback) {\n            m_progressCallback(offset, buff.size());\n        }\n    }\n\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n\n```\n#include \u003cranges\u003e\n\nint iapcontrol::writeRomData(std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e buff)\n{\n    const char funcName[] \u003d \"send data\";\n    size_t offset \u003d 0;\n    const size_t pageSize \u003d BOOT_PAGE_SIZE;\n\n    if (buff.empty()) return -1;\n\n    // We can just name the loop variable \u0027chunk\u0027 now\n    for (auto chunk : buff | std::views::chunk(pageSize)) {\n        if (iapSendData(chunk)) {\n            logInfo(\"[IAP] {} - fail, count: {}\\n\", funcName, offset);\n            return -1;\n        }\n\n        offset +\u003d chunk.size();\n\n        if (m_progressCallback) {\n            m_progressCallback(offset, buff.size());\n        }\n    }\n\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
