      "message": "**Ignored Partial USB Transfers:** Throughout `iapcontrol.cc` (e.g., `iapSendCommand`, `iapSendData`, `iapRecvData`), `libusb_interrupt_transfer` is used. The code currently only checks if `errCode !\u003d 0`. However, USB transfers can succeed partially. If `transferred` is less than `buff.size()`, your protocol state will desync, but the code will silently treat it as a full success. \n\n**Remediation:** Explicitly check that `transferred \u003d\u003d static_cast\u003cint\u003e(buff.size())`. If it is less, treat it as a critical failure or implement a retry mechanism for the remaining bytes.",
