      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Fragile Command-Line Parsing:** The manual iteration through `argv` in `CommandLineManager::parseCommandLine` is brittle. If an unrecognized flag precedes `-F`, the `++i` increments can misalign, potentially causing the tool to parse a flag\u0027s value as the next flag.\n\n**Remediation:** Do not reinvent the wheel for CLI arguments. Use POSIX `getopt()` or `getopt_long()`, which is robust, standard across ChromiumOS host tools, and automatically handles edge cases like merged flags.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 50,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 50,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "eee15e6508ade570d3670bc2f00d613d0a77d9c7",
